
Cipher Text: 

REPEAT: RQYBRPAU

I first tried tackling this problem by finding the biggest repeat in the cipher text which was RQYBRPAU however that keylength of 8 didnt have the highest IOC, so then I wrote an IOC calculator progrma. I worte a java program testing each key length and the index of coincidence I ended up generating through the formula taught in class. I first got for key length of 1 has the IOC of 0.0403 and the best fit key length with the process of doing each key length IOC was key length of 6 which had an IOC of 0.06722. This makes it safe to assume that the key length used in this Vigenere Cipher is 6. Now we split the original cipher text by getting the 6 substrings of the original cipher text. First substring would be all characters 0 + 6 onwards, second substring will be 1+6 onwards and so forth. Each substring now corresponds to one of the key characters. I took each substring and conducted a frequency analysis. When going through the first substring that had every 6th character was shifted by 10 hence for the Key the first letter was J. I continued this process for the other 5 substrings and found the subsequent key letters for the strings were B, E, L, I and Q. When added and modded to the original cipher text I was able to get  the plain text which is pasted below: I had to write several lines of code to automate this deciphiering process. 

Plain Text: 

key: JBELIQ
